<title>INDIA: India Hind Lever 1997 net seen up 22.7 pct.</title>
<headline>India Hind Lever 1997 net seen up 22.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soaps and detergents maker Hindustan Lever's net profit is expected to rise 22.7 percent to 5.08 billion rupees in calendar 1997, a Reuter poll of 28 leading securities and brokerage firms showed.</p>
<p>Projected earnings ranged from 4.14 billion rupees to 5.65 billion rupees against 4.14 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>The company is a subsidiary of Anglo-Dutch conglomerate Unilever Plc.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>HINDUSTAN LEVER ----1997 PAT seen up 22.7%, sales 18.6%</p>
<p>		     Net profit    1996    Net sales	1996</p>
